{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>A stone of charm</b> — missing a [prefix] bet. Likewise <b>her hand to the peg you shall send</b> (Judges 5:26) — although this is not its place, I will explain it because it is obscure, on account of the word תשלחנה, which is in plural language. And its meaning likewise: as <b>her hand to the peg you shall send</b> — the women mentioned in the verse <b>she shall be blessed above women</b> (Judges 5:24), if they do as she did, therefore she shall be blessed more than they. And likewise this: as a precious stone that has charm in the eyes of all who see it, so a bribe has charm in the eyes of its owners — and that is the giver, for because it is forbidden to take it, the taker is not called its owner. Likewise: <b>do not withhold good from its owners</b> (Proverbs 3:27) — that is the taker."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra writes 'missing a kaf' (חסר כ\"ף), but the following argument and the comparison to bet-'owners' throughout strongly suggest he means the prefix bet is missing from אבן (i.e., כאבן חן, 'like a stone of charm'). The text as transmitted may contain a scribal error; translated literally as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:22.059251917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}